First Author: Peyster
Title: An automated computational image analysis pipeline for histological grading of cardiac allograft rejection
Source number: 58

Very short summary: This retrospective multicentre diagnostic study included 2472 cardiac transplant endomyocardial-biopsy slides from 546 recipients at three US centres. The interpretable CACHE-Grader used hand-crafted histological features and support vector machines to classify cellular rejection; on 1447 held-out validation slides, the binary model achieved an AUC of 0.92, 84.5% agreement, 85% sensitivity, and 84% specificity, while the four-grade model achieved 65.9% agreement.

